From 7c1a29b258c9c955e9600163973067b50c52cbd9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 12:33:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: run seed data and new reports on one clock

The engine evaluated on today's date while the seed scenarios stayed in
September 2026, so every asset would drop to 0 thirty days after the last
seeded event (18 Oct), and reports sent without a timestamp were stamped
with a September date.

- seed script rebases scenario dates onto today, preserving the spacing
  between events (--frozen keeps the original dates)
- platform clock is live by default and pinnable via DEFAULT_ANCHOR_TIME;
  tests/conftest.py pins it so the suite passes on any calendar date
- events and what-if simulations without a timestamp use the platform clock
- tests use their own SQLite file, so pytest no longer wipes the demo database
- update three assertions left stale by the risk calibration
  (confidence 86.0, BUS-142 82.0 -> 85.5)
- add tests/test_clock_consistency.py (7 tests)

No scoring weights, thresholds or frontend files are changed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
